WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.570
<i>A customer arrived in
the middle of a terrible storm.</i>

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.790
<i>He drank a lot, often making a scene for the other customers.</i>

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.080
<i>Spending his days scouting the surroundings, he calls himself "Captain".</i>

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.840
<i>One day, this "Captain"
asked me to do him a favor.</i>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.970
<i>He wanted me to look out
for a one-legged sailor.</i>

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.160
It's him!
It's the one-legged sailor!

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:58.950
Wait!

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.820
Dirty beast!

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.590
Let go! Let go!
Let go of me!

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:36.860
Dirty mutt!

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:06.000
Treasure
Island

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.800
Takarajima

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.610
saa ikou

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.610
Come, let's go

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.700
yume ni mita shima heto

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.700
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.540
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.540
Across the waves, on the wind

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.420
umi hedeyou

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.420
We'll travel the oceans

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.340
ikute ni wa

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.340
Many of us

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.340
minna mada shiranai

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.340
Still don't know of

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.090
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.090
The days and nights full of mystery

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.590
matte iru darou

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.590
That await us there

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.100
itsumo shinji you

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.100
We must always have trust

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.350
magokoro wo

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.350
And be sincere

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:49.610
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:49.610
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.740
tade hitotsu no

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.740
I only...

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.160
akogare dake wa

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.160
...have one desire

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.450
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.450
And no one...

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:05.160
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:05.160
...will ever take it away

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.710
tade hitotsu no

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.710
I only...

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.010
akogare dake wa

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.010
...have one desire

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.340
doko no dare ni mo

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.340
And no one...

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:24.270
kese wa shinai sa

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:24.270
...will ever take it away

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:35.250
episode

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:35.250
Who is Black Dog !?

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.070
Good morning, captain!

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.930
Breakfast is ready!

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.500
Are you coming downstairs,
or should I bring it to your room?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:56.250
I'm not hungry. Bring me
three bottles of rum instead.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.630
Alright.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.760
Wait, Jim.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.730
Did someone come to see me this morning?

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.690
No.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.330
What about last night?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.350
Nobody! If someone comes,
I will tell you.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.770
I see...
So it was a dream.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:23.240
In my dream, a storm was raging,
and I heard the sound of footsteps.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.330
Disturbing footsteps...

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.240
I, too, had a strange dream.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.700
It even had the one-legged man in it.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.660
Tell me,
who is the one-legged sailor?

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.630
What do you have to do with him?

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.250
Is he dangerous?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.100
Here's your salary for today.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:49.100
If you ever see that man,
warn me immediately.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.050
I know that much.
I promised you I would.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.730
So if you understand,
don't ask questions.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.480
Go get my rum instead.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.060
Fine!

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:00.510
What? He wants rum
instead of his breakfast?

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.570
He really shouldn't do that.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.650
Even though Dr. Livesey told him
that he drinks too much.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.530
Well, he demanded his rum,
so who cares.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:16.290
Jim, where are you going?

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.090
Out for a bit. Just going for a walk to the village!

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.530
While you're there,
please do the grocery shopping!

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.380
Okay!

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.530
<i>It's only a woman.</i>

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.330
Are you leaving?

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.400
Madam.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.170
Yes?

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:25.110
Don't let anyone enter
my room while I'm gone.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.950
We are a respectable inn.
We'd never allow things like that.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.330
I'll hold you to that.

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:49.260
Jim! Jim!

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:52.530
Jim, what are you doing here?

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.060
It's you, {Squire}Mr. Trelawney!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:55.890
Out shopping?

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.330
Y-Yes, I am.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.020
My mother sent me.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:04.250
By the way, how's your famous customer?
Has he calmed down a bit?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.810
Yes, he's still drinking a lot of rum,

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:09.010
but he hasn't caused any more trouble.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.300
That's good, that's good.
It's better that way.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:18.330
Tell me, have you discovered
if he's a pirate or not?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.690
No, not yet.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:23.460
I see. I don't think that
he will break very easily.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:27.750
If he really is a pirate,
then he will be trialed as one.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:31.130
Even if he escape the gallows,
he'll spend the rest of his days in prison.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:36.860
In any case, come see me or talk to
Dr. Livesey the moment anything happens.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:37.430
Yes, sir!

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.210
Hi, welcome!

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.170
I'll have rum, lad.
Bring me a glass!

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.050
Right away, sir!

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:15.140
It's alright, mother.
I've got it.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:21.100
Here you go.
That'll be six pence.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:23.920
Thank you.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.520
Is Billy here?

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:27.060
Billy?

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.730
He has a scar here.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:33.240
Oh, you mean the captain?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.240
Where's his room?
Take me there.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.200
Wh-Who are you?

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.710
Billy's matey.
And a very good friend of his.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.490
Is his room upstairs?

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:50.420
He isn't here.
He went out for a walk.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:53.530
He isn't here?
Then, all the better...

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:55.510
I'll go wait in his room.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:01.440
Please wait!

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.690
<i>Good, this is the one.
There's no doubt about it!</i>

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.620
Mister!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.530
Laddie!
Go find the key!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.040
The key to his room!

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.600
Out of the question!
This is a respectable inn.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.650
The room of a customer is off-limits!

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.040
I'm one of his mateys!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.070
Mate or not, what's off-limits,
is off-limits!

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.520
He will be returning soon,
so please wait downstairs.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.760
Blast! Alright.
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.440
He's on a walk, is that right?

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:01.630
It's him!

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:07.670
It's been a long time.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:10.210
I'll giv' him a lil' scare.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.080
Is that you, Black Dog?!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.000
Been a while, huh, dear Billy?

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:47.670
Not so fast!

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.730
You not glad to see me?

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.630
We'll discuss things over a drink.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.890
Did the one-legged man send you?

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:09.850
That's not important...

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.840
Just give me what I want nicely...

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.690
...and there'll be no problem.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:17.130
Hey, you two!
Get out of here!

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.150
Right now!

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.530
Jim, quickly now.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.040
But...

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.510
Black Dog, now we have equal chances.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:46.680
Dirty dog!

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:08.930
Stay right there!

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.030
Billy, anything but my life!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:15.960
No mercy!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.320
Jim, run to the village and
bring back a horse or a cart.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:50.240
I must leave here as soon as possible.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.440
<i>Dammit...
Curse you one-legged man.</i>

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.330
<i>Wherever I go, he will always
be searching for me.</i>

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.970
C-Captain!

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.100
Jim, get Dr. Livesey!
Hurry and find him!

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:13.950
On my way!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:27.410
He had an attack. Didn't I tell him
that he drank too much...

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.150
Jim, bring me a basin.

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.200
I'll do a bleeding of him
straight away.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.000
Okay.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.770
<i>A tattoo!</i>

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.260
<i>What's this?</i>

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.000
<i>"Long live Captain Flint!"</i>

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.140
<i>"Your faithful first mate, Billy Bones."</i>

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:00.150
<i>Does it really say "Flint"?
He was a fearsome pirate.</i>

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.110
<i>It's clear now. That means this man is also a pirate.</i>

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.760
Don't give him any more alcohol once he wakes up, got it?

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.550
Next time, his life'll be in danger.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:23.000
Understood.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.110
Farewell.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:26.880
Doctor Livesey!

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.430
Pirates are thrown in prison
or hanged, is that true?

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:34.770
Yes, absolutely.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.690
When he's recovered,
you'll arrest him and judge him?

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:41.520
I am a magistrate,

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.040
but today I came as a doctor.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:47.190
And because of that, I am bound by professional secrecy.

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.010
The doctor says that you should
stay in bed for at least a week.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:14.850
No argument!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.350
Jim, you want to see
what's in my chest?

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.900
Do you have something to break the lock?

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:22.660
Not particularly.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:24.820
Then, did anyone touch it?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.770
Nope.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.110
Good.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:33.370
By the way, Jim, did Black Dog
give you the black spot?

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.070
The black spot?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.160
What's that?

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:41.830
A round and black object,
about this size.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.040
Very good.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.240
That being said, I don't think
that they would go that far.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:50.200
I'll go get your medicine.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.970
I was supposed to give it you
when you woke up.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:54.750
Jim!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:16:00.310
If you go downstairs, bring me some rum.
I'll just have a drop.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.890
You big idiot!

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.520
You can't have anymore alcohol!

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.810
It's because of the rum
that you're like that!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:06.900
So not a drop!

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.280
What's with this bitter medicine?!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:20.200
I imagine not as bitter as the rum, though, right?

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.080
That's enough, you little brat!

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.950
Wretched scoundrel!
You're the one-legged man!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.470
The one-legged man...

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.330
O-One-legged man!

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:24.640
Jim, who is this one-legged man?

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.570
Do you know anything about him?

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.570
I promised not to tell anyone.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.820
I understand...
Well, I won't force you.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.440
But in his current state,

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.820
a simple emotional shock could be fatal.

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:46.020
That's why I should know if this man has any problems.

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:50.450
That's all there is to it.
I will return tomorrow morning.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.420
Doctor Livesey, I'll tell you!

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:58.160
I say that, but I don't know much either.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:03.390
Anyway, he asked me to warn him
if I see a one-legged sailor!

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:04.890
Do you know his name?

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.850
I don't, but he seems very terrifying!

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:11.040
Terrifying you say?

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:13.820
Definitely a pirate like him.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.070
That's what I fear...

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.120
That reminds me...

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.940
I also know of a one-legged man.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.520
Actually, occasionally...

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:33.630
...I go to Bristol for a conference.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:40.590
Upon return, I'd stop at a well-known tavern,
called "The Longue-Vue Tavern"...

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:44.230
...and its owner was a one-legged man.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.540
He was a very jolly man.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:50.920
He used to be the Master Cook
on a large ship...

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:54.990
...and told his customers all sorts of extraordinary stories.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:59.890
Additionally, his wife was a beauty of African descent.

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.420
Her sang and dance were truly wonderful...

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:06.710
Forget that.
But all things considered,

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:11.050
no matter how you looked at it, this man was not the type of person to be a pirate.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:17.710
I'm sorry, I guess that has nothing to do with our current situation.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.290
Isn't it great that you can go outside again?

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:37.730
I sure missed coming down to this cape.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.120
So, Jim, did you bring it with you?

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:40.780
"It" being?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.240
You know, "it"!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.740
No! You're not getting
a single drop of rum!

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:51.330
The Admiral Benbow Inn...

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:54.960
You gave it a very fine name.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.840
A long time ago,
my father was in the navy.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:03.390
He served under the orders of the Admiral Benbow.
That's why it was named that.

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:04.800
I see...

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:08.670
You know, I may have met your father.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.360
When I was with old Flint,

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:15.000
we were in a battle on the China sea.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.440
Against the tremendous fleet of the Admiral Benbow.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.440
What memories...

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:22.720
Flint was the captain
and I was his first mate.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:25.320
Together, we scoured the seven seas.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:31.290
In the end, the only place for a true sailor to die, is out on sea.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:44.300
Jim!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.260
Where are you going in this fog?

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.730
Hey, Lilly!
I'm going down to the village!

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:54.930
There's a stagecoach
that came from Bristol.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.520
I'm going to see if I can find some customers!

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.850
See you later!

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.660
Welcome, please come to the Admiral Benbow Inn!

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.620
Our stew is famous!

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:17.630
Come to the Admiral Benbow!
The Admiral Benbow Inn!

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.130
Darn...

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.550
Please be welcome!

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:26.800
Please be welcome!

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.900
Excuse me, is someone there?

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:43.680
I am a poor blind man...

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:47.820
Would you be kind enough
to tell me where I am?

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:51.280
You are in the main square
of Black Hill village.

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:54.920
Oh, the main square.
I see.

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:57.400
Young man,

00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:01.440
excuse me for asking this,
but can you give me your hand...

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:05.680
...and guide me to the creek?

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:06.590
Of course.

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:07.630
Follow me.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:12.970
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:17.270
Laddie, bring me to Billy!

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:27.330
To      be        continued

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:33.170
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:33.170
Hey sea breeze

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.980
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.980
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:45.190
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:45.190
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:50.630
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:50.630
A word to my dear mother

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:56.040
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:56.040
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:22:56.040 --> 00:23:01.500
kaban ippai no

00:22:56.040 --> 00:23:01.500
And that my bag filled

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:07.130
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:07.130
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:12.990
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:12.990
Will be brought back

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:19.580
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:19.580
The sunset on my back

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:25.470
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:25.470
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:35.190
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:35.190
I blow out a whistle

00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:43.230
Eventually, the old beggar hands Billy Bones the Black Spot.

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:50.060
The Black Spot gives other pirates the right to kill whoever carries it—anytime and anywhere.

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.110
Before they come,

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:55.000
Billy entrusts me with the key to his chest.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:59.790
Then, the one-legged man gives
the orders to attack Billy Bones.

00:24:00.310 --> 00:24:03.240
Next time on Treasure Island:
"The Thrown Down Crutches"

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:04.300
Don't miss it!

